in 2016) has won the Miles Franklin Award.\\n\\nRepeat ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miles_Franklin_Award\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2010s Baillie Gifford Prize winner and shortlist\\n\\n| Year | Author | Title | Result | Ref. |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2010 | | Nothing to Envy: Ordinary Lives in North Korea | | |\\n| 2010 | | Alex's Adventures in Numberland: Dispatches from the Wonderful World of Mathematics | | |\\n| 2010 | | Blood Knots: On Fathers, Friendship and Fishing | | |\\n| 2010 | | Too Big to Fail: The ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baillie_Gifford_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... Camera (winner of the 2012 Green Rose Prize in Poetry from New Issues Press), Carrier Wave (winner of the 2006 Colorado Prize for Poetry from the Center for Literary Publishing at Colorado State University), and the digital chapbook The Tallest Building in America (Floating Wolf Quarterly 2014). An ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... A selection of his poetry is collected in Desire Never … Read More\\n\\nColm Toíbín\\n\\nColm Toíbín is the author of six novels, including The Master, winner of the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award and shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, as well as winner of the LA Times ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigati