gation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... Major Jackson\\n\\nOctober 27, 2021\\n\\nMajor Jackson is the author of five books of poetry, including The Absurd Man (2020), Roll Deep (2015), Holding Company (2010), Hoops (2006) and Leaving Saturn (2002), which won the Cave Canem Poetry Prize for a first book of poems. His edited volumes ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... Kalau Almony, Honford Star, 2024)\\n* 2012 (147th) - Maki Kashimada, Touring the Land of the Dead (trans. Haydn Trowell, Europa Editions, 2021)\\n* 2013 (149th) - Kaori Fujino, Nails and Eyes (trans. Kendall Heitzman, Pushkin Press, 2023)\\n* 2013 (150th) - Hiroko Oyamada, The Hole (trans. David Boyd, New Directions Publishing, 2020)\\n* 2014 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akutagawa_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Life Apart (2010), which won the Writers' Guild of Great Britain Award for Best Fiction Book; The Lives of Others (2014), which was shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize and the Costa Best Novel Award, and won the Royal Society of Literature's Encore Award; and A ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/meet-the-2021-literary-awards-judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d33\"},\"ref\":\"d33\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sites and Transits (Temple University Press, 2006); Studies in the Literary Imagination (SLI, Vol. 37.1, Spring 2004) on Asian American Literature; MELUS (Winter 2008) on the topic of \\\"Alien/Asian\\\"; and Modern Fiction Studies on the topic of \\\"Theorizing Asian American Fiction\\\" (2010). Articles have appeared or ... \",\"title\":\"https://authorsguild.org/about/team/council-bios/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"ab4b9fc3cd3b946940e2e86569419abb925dcee38f87af333220318c860138e3\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"91254dfe07904363cf47d484664f2ba7603086db5c5434c0373f43b3af8dd9c3\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_7b76593a677b4997a2c2872a"},{"content":"I have strong evidence about Chigozie Obioma (born in Akure, Nigeria; both novels shortlisted for the Booker Prize, translated into 30 languages). But the Booker Prize was established in 1969, not the 2000s. The puzzle says \"the award itself\" was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully.\n\nRe-reading: \"the very award above for which the first book was later in contention\" — this strongly implies the SAME award. The Man Asian Literary Prize (established 2007) fits \"created in the 2000s.\" But Obioma's books were shortlisted for the Booker Prize, not the Man Asian Literary Prize. Let me reconsider whether the puzzle might involve a different award, or whether I'm misreading. Let me search for awards created in the 2000s that Obioma's books were contenders for, and also reconsider the structure.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma The Fishermen awards shortlisted translated languages\", \"The Fishermen novel 2015 awards nominations translated\", \"Chigozie Obioma awards nominations The Fishermen An Orchestra of Minorities\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_2c2a92a9240444ddb9c494e0","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2015 | Shortlist | Tom McCarthy | Satin Island | Jonathan Cape | * Michael Wood (chair) * John Burnside * Sam Leith * Frances Osborne * Ellah Wakatama Allfrey |\\n| 2015 | Shortlist | Chigozie Obioma | The Fishermen | One | * Michael Wood (chair) * John Burnside * Sam Leith * Frances Osborne * Ellah Wakatama Allfrey |\\n| 2015 | Shortlist | Sunjeev Sahota | The Year of the Runaways ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Niger